Video Three
- git log shows full commit details and git log --oneline shows commits in short form.
- git show shows commit information.
- git branch is used to check all branches.
- git branch file3 creates a new branch named file3.
- The * symbol shows which branch we are currently on.
- git switch file3 is used to switch to another branch.
- git checkout can also be used to switch branches.
- git branch -m newname is used to rename a branch.
- Each branch can have different code changes without directly changing the main branch.
- git merge is used to bring changes from one branch into another.
- git diff shows differences between changes or commits.
- git stash saves temporary changes, and git stash pop brings them back.
- git tag is used to mark a specific version of the project.

